  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' points at the `kibana_sample_data_flights` index, and its time field is `timestamp`. Useful fields include `Carrier`, `Cancelled` (true/false), `FlightDelay`, `AvgTicketPrice`, `Origin`/`Dest` and `DistanceKilometers`.\n2. **Dashboard:** I created 'S4-f2d1f199 Flights' with exactly two panels: a line chart of flight count over time, and a bar chart of flight count by carrier (top 10 carriers).\n   URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/s4-f2d1f199-flights-9d7d1736e026\n3. **Alert rule:** I created 'S4-f2d1f199 Cancelled flights' as an Elasticsearch query rule. It counts flights where `Cancelled` is true, checks every minute, and fires when there are more than 10 in a 5-minute window. I created it already enabled, so it didn't need a separate enable step.\n4. **Edit and read-back:** I updated the carrier panel with the title 'Flights by carrier'. I had already given it that title when I built the dashboard, so the edit didn't change anything visible. Reading the rule back shows it is enabled, with status \"ok\".\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
